      "final_message": "The key is `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\nThe call chain:\n\n1. `service.checkout(\"7781\")` calls `write_audit(\"order\", \"7781\")` in `audit.py`.\n2. `write_audit` builds the key with `_format_key(kind, ident)` (`audit.py:11`).\n3. `_format_key` returns `f\"{AUDIT_PREFIX}-{kind.upper()}-{ident}\"`, and `AUDIT_PREFIX` is `\"AUD\"` in `config.py`.\n\nSo the result is `AUD-ORDER-7781`. I also ran `write_audit('order', '7781')` directly, and the only key in the returned log was `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\n`decoy_metrics.py` looks similar but uses the `MET` prefix and writes to a metrics dict, not the audit log. `decoy_cache.py` never touches the audit log either.\n\nANSWER: AUD-ORDER-7781",
      "final_message_source": "stdout_response",
