      "final_message": "I added the `--dry-run` flag to `cli_tool.py`. With it, the tool prints `DRY RUN: would {action} {path}` and exits without creating or deleting anything. Without it, the tool does exactly what it did before.\n\nThere's no `test_public.py` in this directory, so I checked it by hand with a throwaway file, `x.tmp`, which is gone now:\n\n| Command | Output | File afterwards |\n|---|---|---|\n| create, `--dry-run` | `DRY RUN: would create x.tmp` | not created |\n| create | `DONE: create x.tmp` | created |\n| delete, `--dry-run` | `DRY RUN: would delete x.tmp` | still there |\n| delete | `DONE: delete x.tmp` | removed |\n\nDONE: Added a `--dry-run` store_true flag to cli_tool.py that prints `DRY RUN: would {action} {path}` and skips the file change; normal behavior is unchanged.",
